116
00:05:49,610 --> 00:05:51,530
And it still pulled it off perfectly.

117
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:54,930
Next, let's have Qwen generate a shadow puppetry animation editor.

118
00:05:54,930 --> 00:05:58,590
Users can place silhouette props onto the stage.

119
00:05:58,590 --> 00:06:03,830
You can set the position, scale, rotation, and transparency of objects using the timeline.

120
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:06,070
Let's create a 10-second looping animation.

121
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:07,720
On the left, we have the prop library.

122
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:12,140
Elements like the moon, windows, and bridges can be added directly to the stage.

123
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:14,060
In the center is the stage, which has a paper-like texture.

124
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:17,020
And on the right, we have the properties panel.

125
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:19,200
And down here is the timeline.

126
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,600
Select a silhouette.

127
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:26,660
You can adjust its size, rotation angle, and transparency.

128
00:06:26,660 --> 00:06:30,580
You can also control whether it's on the top layer or the bottom layer.

129
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:33,870
The key to making it move is the keyframe.

130
00:06:33,870 --> 00:06:35,870
At the 0-second mark, I'll place an umbrella.

131
00:06:37,030 --> 00:06:45,450
Then at the 5-second mark, I'll make the umbrella bigger and add another keyframe.

132
00:06:46,610 --> 00:06:49,770
And finally, at the 10-second mark, shrink the umbrella.

133
00:06:50,389 --> 00:06:51,389
Press play,

134
